KG42.register("rules-4cbb271302ef25eff43d21a2",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"Selling surplus energy to the MGO produces prosumer revenue p_s(E_n^g − x_n). Scope: Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0. A prosumer's energy purchase from the MGO has the monetary term p_b(E_n^g − x_n), represented as negative revenue in its utility. Scope: Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. | Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-x-n","symbol":"x_n","meaning":"Energy consumed by prosumer n in a time slot; the source defines the traded net energy as E_n^g - x_n. In this payment rule it is the consumption quantity entering the settlement term.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy consumption values for prosumer n in a time slot; numeric bounds are not specified by this rule's attached evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-ps","symbol":"p_s","meaning":"Internal selling price set by the MGO, used for seller revenue in the surplus branch E_n^g - x_n > 0.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-pb","symbol":"p_b","meaning":"Internal buying price set by the MGO, used for the buyer negative-revenue term in the nonpositive-net branch E_n^g - x_n \u003c= 0.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-Eng","symbol":"E_n^g","meaning":"Energy produced by prosumer n in the relevant time slot; it enters the net traded energy E_n^g - x_n used by the payment term.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Selling surplus energy to the MGO produces prosumer revenue p_s(E_n^g − x_n). Scope: Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0.","expression":"p_s (E_n^g - x_n)  for  E_n^g - x_n > 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-x-n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R010-ps","v141-c-R010-Eng"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"A prosumer's energy purchase from the MGO has the monetary term p_b(E_n^g − x_n), represented as negative revenue in its utility. Scope: Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","expression":"p_b (E_n^g - x_n)  for  E_n^g - x_n \u003c= 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-x-n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R010-pb","v141-c-R010-Eng"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"revenue of trading energy. In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for differ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for different time slots, so we have extended the utility function as a piecewise function: U_n(x_n) = { k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_s(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_b(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (1) In (1), U_n(x_n) is the utility of prosumer n, k_n ln(1 + x_n) is the utility that the prosumer n achieves from consuming energy x_n. Note that k_n is the preference parameter of prosumer n, which changes with behavioral characteristics of the prosumer. It is shown in (1) that a prosumer with higher k_n would be more interested in consuming more x_n to attain its maximum utility level compared to a prosumer with lower preference. The ln(·) function has been widely used in economics for modeling the preference ordering of users and for decision making, and also recently been shown to be suitable for designing the utility for power consumers [23]. p_s(E_n^g − x_n) is the revenue that the prosumer receives from selling the rest of its energy, whereas p_b(E_n^g − x_n) is the negative revenue when the prosumer buys energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","quote":"p_s(E_n^g − x_n) is the revenue that the prosumer receives from selling the rest of its energy"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","quote":"If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","quote":"whereas p_b(E_n^g − x_n) is the negative revenue when the prosumer buys energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","quote":"Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"7737d5887054020c11347f2ad04c3c53b844a0644887855547c06d859bfd3f61","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The rule's settlement payment terms are explicitly stated in equation (1) and the net-trade definition: seller revenue p_s(E_n^g - x_n) when E_n^g - x_n > 0, and buyer negative revenue p_b(E_n^g - x_n) when E_n^g - x_n \u003c= 0. The x and theta objects are declared only for these settlement terms and are bound to the frozen execution.energy_trade -> settlement.payment edge. B evidence remains unreviewed; no source-audit conclusion is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-x-n","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"x_n is the prosumer consumption entering the net traded quantity E_n^g - x_n on execution.energy_trade; the same net quantity is priced for settlement.payment through the frozen links edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-ps","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"p_s is the internal selling price applied to the prosumer's surplus trade: the surplus is executed in execution.energy_trade and paid in settlement.payment via the frozen edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-pb","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"p_b is the internal buying price applied to the prosumer's nonpositive net-energy trade: the trade executes in execution.energy_trade and its monetary term is settled in settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-Eng","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"E_n^g is the prosumer's produced energy; E_n^g - x_n is the traded surplus or deficit on execution.energy_trade and the quantity multiplied by the price in settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"The surplus-sale payment term applies when positive net energy from execution.energy_trade is settled at settlement.payment, exactly through the frozen links edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"The buyer-branch negative-revenue term applies when nonpositive net energy from execution.energy_trade is settled at settlement.payment, exactly through the frozen links edge."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
